{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791668718,"nonce":"ohPOB9azbsByJA0wLv5R6ydzAhk=","title":"Reactive JSX runtime: sources, regions, control flow and owners","message":"adapters/jsx built a description once and could not change it. A view that updates needs a way to say what changes, without a virtual DOM, and a lifetime for what a component makes.\n\nDesign\n- A source is a signal, a computed value or a function. A prop that is one follows it (class, attributes, style whole or per property); a child that is one is a region between two comment placeholders, text rewritten in place and anything else built anew in a fresh owner after the last ends. The react-jsx transform evaluates props eagerly, so a function is how a view says \"read this again\", as a Solid view without its compiler does.\n- Owners: a mounted view is one owner; each region, For item and Provider has its own. signal, computed, memo, effect and onCleanup belong to the current owner and end with it. A region that makes an owner per rebuild leaves them unattached from the parent, since a Scope cannot unregister a cleanup, and ends the last itself.\n- Control flow as components that build themselves in place: Show (a function child is given the value), Switch and Match, For (built once per item, found by identity, moved rather than rebuilt, an index function), createContext with Provider and useContext.\n- mount() for a view that updates and returns its disposer; render() stays for one that cannot, and a source in it is a TypeError that names mount().\n\nFound on the way\n- A computed value has no equality cutoff: what reads one reruns each time it is recomputed, even to the same value. Show and Switch would have rebuilt on every change of a truthy value, so they use memo, a signal an effect keeps and a signal does cut off. The Show test caught it.\n- An effect created while another is running first runs after it, in the same pass. A prop is therefore set at once and then bound, so a ref sees it; a nested region's content appears when the outer update finishes.\n\nNot covered: Dynamic, Portal, error boundaries, an Index that keeps by position, transitions between regions' content.","files":null}]}